	(text "Team decision 2026-11-01: MPR121 stays on an Adafruit 1982 module in sockets J7/J9, I2C through Qwiic.\nThis differs from the brief's integrated controller. Pin order read from Adafruit's board file.\nRows sit 15.24 mm apart. J9 pin 1 at x = 1.27 mm, J7 pin 1 at x = 8.89 mm from the module's left edge.\nR90 ties ADDR to the module's 3V3 output, moving it from 0x5A to 0x5B (no clash with DRV2605L).\nR91-R93 (DNP) let you hard-wire power and I2C instead of using a Qwiic cable.\nE1-E12 are placeholders: the layout engineer replaces each with a copper electrode.\nWheel diameter and overlay thickness are not final: layout and mechanical dependency."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "56c81d69-4b15-5f3d-9be8-d9c735651967")
	)
